1
00:00:00,870 --> 00:00:02,420
Juzo Ogami.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:06,750
A member of Z.O.O., the industry's
third-ranked old-guard organization.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,550
Formerly the number one hitman
in the business…

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:12,470
until he vanished without warning.

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:15,390
Mission success rate: 100%.

6
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:20,390
However, he refuses any job targeting
women, children or civilians.

7
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:23,310
Preferred cigarette brand: Blue Apple.

8
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:25,110
Whiskey of choice: Laphroaig.

9
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:27,270
Hm…

10
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:32,860
Marksmanship, hand-to-hand combat,
knife fighting… all first-rate.

11
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:36,160
Weapon of choice: P210.

12
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:40,250
He's ambidextrous, and even when
he fires with his left hand…

13
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,410
he can hit with the 
precision of a sniper rifle.

14
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:45,250
That's how it ended up nicknamed
the Devil's Left Hand.

15
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,290
No way.

16
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:55,050
Almost there.

17
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:59,060
VERSUS THE RINDOU BROTHERS
SATURDAY, MAY 30th

18
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:41,280
So, it ends before I even use
my real weapon.

19
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,410
How anticlimactic!

20
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:57,880
So, have we contacted their parents?

21
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,880
Not yet.

22
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:01,050
Word is that someone upstairs
is holding that up.

23
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:03,890
Why?

24
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:04,970
Beats me.

25
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,310
RYO SHIRAISHI
WHAT ARE YOU GONNA DO FOR DINNER?
ARE YOU EATING WITH YOUR FRIENDS?

26
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:08,810
LET'S SEE…

27
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:13,570
All three of you, come back safe!

28
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:21,820
Naturally, I'm gonna beat
the shit outta you!

29
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,200
Hah!

30
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,580
He's good.

31
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:29,210
A straight shoot-out
puts me at a disadvantage.

32
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,090
Good.

33
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:39,340
Got my magazine back, too.

34
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:42,140
Nekota's been a damn lifesaver today.

35
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:43,640
Hey! Are you hurt?

36
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,560
Huh? A-A security guard?

37
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,890
The place is closed today, you know!
How did you even get in?

38
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:50,690
Uh, well…

39
00:03:50,690 --> 00:03:53,440
And there are strange
 explosions going off!

40
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,320
It's dangerous here, so get out! Hurry!

41
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:59,820
Damn, I thought he'd emptied
the place out before luring me in here!

42
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:02,240
Wait! You'll drag a civilian into this!

43
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,780
That's your policy, isn't it?

44
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:07,830
Not mine.

45
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,410
With their positions…

46
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,460
if Juzo dodges, the guard gets hit!

47
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:12,120
Hah!

48
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,750
That's low, you bastard!

49
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:18,550
What… the hell?

50
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:27,100
Shooting bullets out of the air
with other bullets is unthinkable!

51
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:30,480
The only man capable
of such an inhuman trick is…

52
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:33,690
Ah, now I see. It all fits.

53
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:36,270
Noren Mitsuoka. Mitsuoka Pharmaceuticals.

54
00:04:36,270 --> 00:04:38,230
And when I looked into you…

55
00:04:38,230 --> 00:04:40,740
I thought it was strange that you
had the exact same name…

56
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,450
as that legendary hitman.

57
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:45,240
But the age difference was so great,
I assumed you were someone else.

58
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:49,790
As hard as it is to believe, this is
no mere case of identical names.

59
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,000
You are…

60
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,330
Juzo Ogami himself!

61
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:54,420
He figured it out?

62
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,630
This is why I asked…

63
00:04:56,630 --> 00:05:00,000
if you were sure you didn't wanna change
your name before enrolling!

64
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,300
How was I supposed to know
it'd come to this?

65
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,720
The job was supposed to be quick!

66
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:09,060
Just sneak into a middle school and 
do some internal recon!

67
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,430
Yeah, it was.

68
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,100
Wrong!

69
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:17,150
I do have a connection to Juzo Ogami,
but I'm not the legendary hitman himself!

70
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:19,940
I'm…

71
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,530
My wife's out of town today.

72
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:22,440
You know…

73
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,700
You're shameless!

74
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:25,200
I'm Juzo Ogami's…

75
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,860
secret love child!

76
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,530
What are you talking about?

77
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:32,040
Well, I'm off to Tokyo
to make it even bigger! Take care!

78
00:05:32,370 --> 00:05:33,500
You're shameless!

79
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,750
After he got bored
of my mother, his mistress…

80
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:39,170
he found himself a younger woman
and vanished from our lives!

81
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,550
I swore revenge against him.

82
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:45,300
So, I deliberately took the same name
and chose the same path.

83
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,470
By making a name for myself,
I knew that someday,

84
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:51,350
when I finally ran into my scumbag
old man, I'd say this to his face…

85
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:54,730
"Why the hell did you abandon us?"

86
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:58,270
There are so many holes
in this story, old man!

87
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:01,520
I see.

88
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:03,400
- I understand.
- Huh?

89
00:06:03,690 --> 00:06:06,150
You've had a hard life, too, haven't you?

90
00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:07,410
He bought it?

91
00:06:07,410 --> 00:06:08,660
I know how you feel!

92
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:12,490
For those of us in the underworld,
life is full of misery!

93
00:06:12,490 --> 00:06:16,410
And the people we cross paths with?
Every last one of them is scum!

94
00:06:16,410 --> 00:06:18,620
<i>Boss, you just got classified as scum.</i>

95
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:21,380
You must want to murder
your father something fierce!

96
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,880
Y-Yeah.

97
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:26,340
Well, we brothers have had
our share of troubles, too.

98
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:30,430
Long ago, my younger brother Eiji
wasn't the silent type he is now.

99
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:32,220
Is "silent" really the word for that?

100
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:37,350
Until we were swept up
in a certain incident…

101
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:39,600
I was just a kid who loved magic tricks.

102
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,610
And my brother was just a kid
who loved sports.

103
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,860
We were no different
from any other pair of brothers.

104
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:48,490
Were you watching?

105
00:06:48,490 --> 00:06:49,660
Did you see that shot?

106
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:51,780
I saw it! Nice one!

107
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,830
Oops.

108
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:59,920
Getting sentimental
won't do either of us any good.

109
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:05,420
Anyway, my little brother Eiji is the most
precious person in the world to me.

110
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:10,510
Noren is going to become
part of his happiness.

111
00:07:10,890 --> 00:07:12,470
And the secrets of Mitsuoka…

112
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:15,430
may even hold the possibility
of restoring my brother to his old self.

113
00:07:16,470 --> 00:07:18,730
Seems we both have our reasons…

114
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:21,440
but I cannot afford to lose.

115
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:24,360
A lighter?

116
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:28,360
I told you, didn't I?
My specialty is hypnosis.

117
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,240
And this is…

118
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,160
my true weapon.

119
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:43,290
Hah! So, that's the deal!

120
00:07:43,290 --> 00:07:46,170
The security guard just happened
to show up at the perfect time…

121
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:48,130
because he was already
under this guy's control!

122
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:49,720
Sorry about this!

123
00:07:55,970 --> 00:07:58,100
Okay, sure, you gave me a little scare.

124
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:59,350
But is that all you've got?

125
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:02,190
One civilian puppet is no sweat.

126
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,650
One? Oh, no, no.

127
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:09,150
Did you think I only started
using hypnosis after declaring war?

128
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,110
Wrong.

129
00:08:11,110 --> 00:08:14,280
I knew you would make it this far.

130
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:15,490
TAKUMI
YUTO NAKAMURA
CHIHIRO FUJIWARA
RINA
NAOKI TAKAMURA

131
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:17,870
The preparations were already complete.

132
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:19,200
CALLING…

133
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:22,710
A long, long time ago!

134
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:29,590
Don't tell me…

135
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,570
TENMA TENDO
CALLING…

136
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:50,860
Oh, Ogami? Where are you?

137
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:53,320
Sorry. I got careless!
Get out of there right now!

138
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:56,070
And stay away
from any crowds of civilians!

139
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:57,830
They're under hypnosis!

140
00:08:57,830 --> 00:08:59,540
Yeah? Okay. Got it.

141
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:02,870
That was way too casual! Do you
actually understand what I'm saying?

142
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:04,250
I said I got it.

143
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:09,380
After seeing stuff like those exploding
golf shots, I know this isn't normal.

144
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:11,260
And yeah, I know I might die.

145
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:14,090
But I won't run away.

146
00:09:14,090 --> 00:09:14,970
Seriously?

147
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:17,890
Don't underestimate athletes.

148
00:09:18,430 --> 00:09:22,020
In any pro sport, the top-tier guys
may not literally be risking their lives,

149
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:24,690
but they put their lives
on the line anyway.

150
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:29,070
I'm aiming to be a super-elite
triple-threat phenom, remember?

151
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:33,650
If I can't cross one or two or three lines
between life and death, what good am I?

152
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:37,240
So, yeah, I'll leave your end to you.

153
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:37,990
Huh?

154
00:09:37,990 --> 00:09:38,820
Hey!

155
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,700
This is a risk…

156
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,500
but it's also an opportunity.

157
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:46,120
I want to become a triple-threat
superman capable of pulling off…

158
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,080
something that seems imposisble.

159
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:52,170
And to do that, I've developed
 everything I could possibly need…

160
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:57,680
in the most efficient way possible,
based on common sense and solid logic.

161
00:09:58,090 --> 00:09:59,430
I've gotten results.

162
00:09:59,430 --> 00:10:01,390
I don't think I've been wrong.

163
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:05,180
But… to accomplish something
that defies common sense…

164
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:08,350
I've also had the feeling that 
I might need something more.

165
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:10,860
So, this is a chance.

166
00:10:11,190 --> 00:10:13,780
If I can make it through 
this life-and-death contest…

167
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:16,610
then no matter what I face
in the future, I'll be able to say…

168
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,700
"Compared to that, this is nothing."

169
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:22,790
I'll know it for sure.

170
00:10:22,790 --> 00:10:27,000
I'm absolutely going to become
a triple-threat superman!

171
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,470
Hey, Patchwork Giant!

172
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:46,680
Let's play some sports.

173
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:23,970
Dine and dash… Unforgivable!

174
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:33,900
All right, then! Let's kick this off!

175
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,950
Holy crap, this is scary!

176
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:51,540
Yeah, he's an evil creep
who kidnaps people,

177
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:54,960
but he's also seriously firing exploding
golf balls at me! Is he nuts?

178
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:56,920
Huh?

179
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,170
"Whock"?

180
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:01,050
Huh?

181
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,220
How'd it come from behind me?

182
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,680
No, wait, in golf, that's…

183
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:09,230
backspin!

184
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,440
Hah!

185
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:14,690
I knew it!

186
00:12:15,150 --> 00:12:16,570
He switched clubs!

187
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:19,860
A full set? Since when?

188
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:35,500
Man, that's insane! He's hitting them
with those skinny little sticks…

189
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:38,800
and make them curve and 
drop however he wants?

190
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:40,050
Fine then!

191
00:12:58,190 --> 00:13:00,400
Get back here…

192
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:08,410
D-Dammit!

193
00:13:13,370 --> 00:13:14,960
There are too many of them!

194
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:18,290
I'm worried about Tenma, but I can't go
to him with this mob in tow!

195
00:13:18,290 --> 00:13:20,210
Right now, all I can do is run!

196
00:13:32,350 --> 00:13:34,560
Crap! I ended up outside!

197
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,490
Looks like somebody called it in.

198
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:45,400
I mean, yeah, with this much commotion…

199
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:47,160
No, hang on.

200
00:13:48,950 --> 00:13:50,080
That's not it.

201
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:52,660
Take this!

202
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:54,000
They're hypnotized, too?

203
00:13:54,410 --> 00:13:55,080
Hah!

204
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:58,130
That is not what a stretcher is for!

205
00:13:58,750 --> 00:14:00,170
Open up the hose!

206
00:14:01,210 --> 00:14:02,130
Boss!

207
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,380
No, actually…

208
00:14:03,710 --> 00:14:04,550
this helps.

209
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:05,260
Huh?

210
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:09,600
Mind if I borrow that?

211
00:14:12,970 --> 00:14:14,060
Sorry about this!

212
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:19,190
Good thing it's not
the middle of winter, huh?

213
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:20,310
Yeah.

214
00:14:20,310 --> 00:14:21,690
It's a little cold…

215
00:14:21,690 --> 00:14:23,480
but wake the hell up!

216
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:37,120
Okay. That takes care of things for now.

217
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,040
<i>You did it, boss!</i>

218
00:14:41,590 --> 00:14:42,290
Big Sis?

219
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,880
Wh-Wh-What the heck do you have there?

220
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:48,050
No, uh, it's not real!
It's an airsoft gun! Airsoft!

221
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,720
But what are you doing here?

222
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,510
I came because I was worried!

223
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:56,520
More importantly, what is all this?
The whole place is wrecked!

224
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,520
But anyway… just look at this!

225
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:06,240
I will count to three.

226
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:09,610
When I finish counting and 
you hear the lighter close…

227
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:14,580
you will be unable to attack
Kazuma Rindou or Eiji Rindou.

228
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:16,370
Three…

229
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:17,660
Two…

230
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:19,160
One.

231
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,420
You bastard!

232
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:27,720
You're Kazuma Rindou?

233
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:31,390
Disguises are another specialty of mine.

234
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:35,100
Though I must say, it took you
an awfully long time to notice.

235
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:38,730
I can't believe the boss got caught
off guard by that!

236
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,810
This isn't like him!

237
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:42,350
No, wait…

238
00:15:42,350 --> 00:15:43,650
it's the opposite actually!

239
00:15:43,650 --> 00:15:45,900
Things ended up this way because
the boss acted exactly like himself!

240
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,990
If he only had to beat down villains,
he'd be invincible!

241
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:51,160
But he doesn't lay a hand on civilians!

242
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:54,030
He might be a little frosty,
but he's not heartless!

243
00:15:54,030 --> 00:15:57,490
If anything, deep down, he's so kind
you'd never believe he was a hitman!

244
00:15:57,490 --> 00:16:00,750
Lately, he's even started
getting attached to his classmates!

245
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:02,830
That soft side of his…

246
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:07,090
played right into Kazuma Rindou's
hands in the worst way!

247
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,720
He got me dead to rights
with that hypnosis!

248
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,090
I really can't shoot him!

249
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:14,350
Um…

250
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:16,390
maybe the safety's on or something?

251
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,020
Like hell!

252
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:21,100
Don't suddenly go full idiot on me!

253
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:32,320
Yeah, that figures.

254
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:41,410
I can still fire in a direction
that has nothing to do with you.

255
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:42,920
So, yeah, I'm definitely under.

256
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:45,170
I would not recommend that.

257
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:48,130
Don't blame me if a stray bullet
hits an innocent bystander.

258
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:51,840
Well, whatever.

259
00:16:52,170 --> 00:16:53,720
That's just about the right handicap.

260
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:56,760
I guess it's time to show you
just how different our careers really are.

261
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:57,470
Wha…

262
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,470
Wha…

263
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,270
Hah!

264
00:17:05,270 --> 00:17:06,730
He hid.

265
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:08,770
But the outcome will be the same.

266
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:13,570
I can't finish him off with just
my Walther, even while he's hypnotized.

267
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:16,240
That bullet-shooting trick is a nuisance.

268
00:17:16,990 --> 00:17:18,080
Very well.

269
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:21,790
I'll lay one more trap and 
see how he responds!

270
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:29,130
Come on out, Ogami's love child!

271
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:31,960
Right, that was the story!

272
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:36,970
You know what this means, right?
You have three seconds.

273
00:17:37,470 --> 00:17:40,350
You have a policy against
involving civilians in this, don't you?

274
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:44,310
There was still
another hypnotized civilian?

275
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,520
Also, what kind of hostage choice is that?

276
00:17:47,150 --> 00:17:48,810
Doesn't this picture look backward?

277
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:52,190
Fine, fine. I'm coming.

278
00:17:53,110 --> 00:17:54,320
There you are.

279
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,820
Throw your gun over here.

280
00:17:58,780 --> 00:18:01,240
Would you like to hear this man scream?

281
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,660
P-Please help me!

282
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:13,840
Honestly, was that poor aim
or one last little act of spite?

283
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:17,680
Now then…

284
00:18:18,470 --> 00:18:20,850
Any last words?

285
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,680
Yeah. I'm begging you…

286
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:28,350
Take off that disguise.

287
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,570
Very well.

288
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:40,240
Satisfied?

289
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:42,280
Then… die—

290
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:43,660
Oh, that's a relief!

291
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:44,870
Thanks!

292
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:46,460
Even knowing it was fake,

293
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:49,710
I wasn't crazy about punching somebody
wearing Big Sis's face.

294
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,580
Huh?

295
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,920
Now you'd better grit your teeth.

296
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:00,640
Wha…

297
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,640
A sniper? An ally?

298
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,640
No, the bullet came from directly above!

299
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,310
Huh? It can't be!

300
00:19:06,310 --> 00:19:08,390
That stray shot from before?

301
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,480
Wait, did you actually aim that?

302
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,650
That doesn't seem humanly possible!

303
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:19,990
I figured out the trick messing around
during training back in the day.

304
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:23,330
Well, it's not like shooting normally.

305
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:25,910
My hit rate's only about 70%
on a good day.

306
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,120
That's still not humanly possible!

307
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:28,960
Again!

308
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:31,330
I was aiming for the stretcher.

309
00:19:31,330 --> 00:19:34,550
I fired three shots,
so I figured one of 'em would hit.

310
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:38,010
And at the foot of the stretcher
is a detonator.

311
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:42,930
Lock picks, mini bombs
and a bunch of useless…

312
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:46,640
When I hid a minute ago,
I set both of them up.

313
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:48,390
Oh, got it!

314
00:19:48,390 --> 00:19:50,230
So, what's gonna happen?

315
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:52,190
Just watch.

316
00:19:52,190 --> 00:19:54,440
What have you been
muttering about over there?

317
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:01,660
And what is that supposed to be?

318
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:05,410
I said I was gonna beat
the shit outta you, remember?

319
00:20:05,410 --> 00:20:08,660
I wanted to do it full force
from my end…

320
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:09,910
but, well, whatever.

321
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:12,920
You can come over here
and take your beating.

322
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:19,300
Wha…

323
00:22:14,330 --> 00:22:15,580
You…

324
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:17,870
I can't believe it!

325
00:22:17,870 --> 00:22:22,340
Is this what you predicted would happen
when you fired into the sky?

326
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:24,340
Hm? Well, more or less.

327
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:27,840
When I fired,
I was only aiming for the stretcher.

328
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:30,890
After that, I calculated backward
as I moved.

329
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:37,270
I mean, that's how I can explain it, but I
wasn't thinking it through that precisely.

330
00:22:37,270 --> 00:22:39,400
It was half-assed. Totally winging it.

331
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,770
What is he?

332
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,400
It isn't just that he's skilled!

333
00:22:44,690 --> 00:22:46,570
The sheer amount of experience…

334
00:22:46,570 --> 00:22:48,530
The depth of his strength…

335
00:22:49,030 --> 00:22:51,120
He's in a different league!

336
00:22:53,790 --> 00:22:55,790
But it's too late now!

337
00:22:55,790 --> 00:22:56,540
What?

338
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:00,710
Noren Mitsuoka is already hypnotized.

339
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:06,300
When she awakens, she will fall in love
with the first person she sees!

340
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:07,300
What?

341
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:08,630
Dammit!

342
00:23:09,050 --> 00:23:10,840
Struggle all you like.

343
00:23:11,180 --> 00:23:13,220
Noren's fate will be the same…

344
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:16,140
either way.

345
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:22,940
Tenma! Tenma!

346
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,070
Please be okay!

347
00:23:33,330 --> 00:23:34,330
Noren…

348
00:23:34,990 --> 00:23:38,160
Don't wake up yet!

